   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "<p>Is there a reason you are using pointers and allocation? Else its as simple as </p>\n\n<pre><code>Class a1;\n...\nClass b1 = a1;\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>There is no need here for a delete.</p>\n\n<p>If you need to keep the structure as it is you need to do</p>\n\n<pre><code>Class *a1 = new Class();\nClass *b1 = new Class(*a1);\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>or </p>\n\n<pre><code>Class *a1 = new Class();\nClass *b1 = new Class();\n*b1 = *a1;\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>This assumes you have a valid copy-constructor ( e.g #1) or assignment operator (e.g #2)</p>\n\n<p>p.s: try to use <code>std::unique_ptr</code> instead of raw pointers to be safer.</p>\n"
  },
